      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>One of the two homilies on Melchizedek's origin attributed to <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3255CyrilI">Cyril I</t:persName>. Both homilies according to <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/TQ2NBVAC"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Dillmann1866Chrestomathia"/><title level="m">Chrestomathia Aethiopica edita et glossario explanata</title><editor><forename>Christian Friedrich August</forename><surname>Dillmann</surname></editor><pubPlace>Lipsiae</pubPlace><publisher>T. O. Weigel</publisher><date>1866</date><note type="url">https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_V2XoxZmczckC</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Literature</note><note type="tag">bm:Dillmann1866Chrestomathia</note></note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Literature</note><note type="tag">bm:Dillmann1866Chrestomathia</note></t:bibl> were translated from the Greek,
               but the original is lost and the Ethiopic version is the only known one, see
                     <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/4TZ6V4PR"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:CPG3"/><title level="m">Clavis patrum Graecorum, III: A Cyrillo Alexandrino ad Iohannem Damascenum</title><title type="short">CPG</title><title level="s">Corpus Christianorum</title><author><forename>Maurice</forename><surname>Geerard</surname></author><pubPlace>Turnhout</pubPlace><publisher>Brepols</publisher><date>1979</date><series><title level="s">Corpus Christianorum</title></series><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:CPG3</note></note><note type="tag">bm:CPG3</note></t:bibl>. Its Gǝʿǝz versions is known to be transmitted as
               part of <t:title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3309Qerellos">Qerǝllos</t:title> or along the <t:title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2365Storyo">Story of Melchizedek</t:title> .
               <t:note>Note that the attribution of the homily to <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3261Cyrilof">Qerǝllos</t:persName> in <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/M67R9PWF"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Pogossian2021Armenia"/><title level="a">Armeno-Aethiopica in the Middle Ages: Geography, Tales of Christianization, Calendars, and Anti-Dyophysite Polemics in the First Millennium</title><title type="short">Armeno-Aethiopica in the Middle Ages</title><title level="j">Aethiopica</title><author><forename>Zaroui</forename><surname>Pogossian</surname></author><date>2022</date><biblScope unit="volume">24</biblScope><note type="accessed">2024-11-25T18:36:09Z</note><note type="url">https://journals.sub.uni-hamburg.de/aethiopica/article/view/1627</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Pogossian2021Armenia</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Pogossian2021Armenia</note><t:citedRange/></t:bibl> has not been corroborated  elsewhere outside of the article.
               </t:note>
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
